Chapter: BleAtt

 Bluetooth Low Energy ATT (Attribute Protocol) and its L2CAP wrapper --
 the layer every BLE sensor and actuator speaks (GATT is built directly
 on ATT). A PDU is a one-byte opcode followed by opcode-specific fields;
 attribute handles are 16-bit little-endian. ATT runs over the fixed
 L2CAP channel 0x0004. This chapter builds the common client and server
 PDUs and the L2CAP frame around them.

Section: Opcodes

  att-op-error : Integer = #01
  att-op-exchange-mtu-request : Integer = #02
  att-op-read-request : Integer = #0A
  att-op-read-response : Integer = #0B
  att-op-write-request : Integer = #12
  att-op-write-response : Integer = #13
  att-op-notification : Integer = #1B
  att-op-indication : Integer = #1D
  att-op-write-command : Integer = #52

  l2cap-cid-att : Integer = #04

Section: Helpers

  att-u16-le : Integer -> List Integer
  att-u16-le (v) = [bit-and v 255, bit-and (bit-shru v 8) 255]

Section: Client PDUs

  att-exchange-mtu-request : Integer -> List Integer
  att-exchange-mtu-request (mtu) = [att-op-exchange-mtu-request] & att-u16-le mtu

  att-read-request : Integer -> List Integer
  att-read-request (handle) = [att-op-read-request] & att-u16-le handle

  att-write-request : Integer, List Integer -> List Integer
  att-write-request (handle) (value) = [att-op-write-request] & att-u16-le handle & value

  att-write-command : Integer, List Integer -> List Integer
  att-write-command (handle) (value) = [att-op-write-command] & att-u16-le handle & value

Section: Server PDUs

  att-read-response : List Integer -> List Integer
  att-read-response (value) = [att-op-read-response] & value

  att-notification : Integer, List Integer -> List Integer
  att-notification (handle) (value) = [att-op-notification] & att-u16-le handle & value

  att-indication : Integer, List Integer -> List Integer
  att-indication (handle) (value) = [att-op-indication] & att-u16-le handle & value

  att-error-response : Integer, Integer, Integer -> List Integer
  att-error-response (request-op) (handle) (error-code) =
   [att-op-error, request-op] & att-u16-le handle & [error-code]

Section: L2CAP Frame

 An L2CAP basic frame: a two-byte payload length, a two-byte channel
 id, then the payload. ATT uses channel 0x0004.

  l2cap-frame : Integer, List Integer -> List Integer
  l2cap-frame (cid) (payload) =
   att-u16-le (list-length payload) & att-u16-le cid & payload

  att-l2cap : List Integer -> List Integer
  att-l2cap (pdu) = l2cap-frame l2cap-cid-att pdu
